Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||10-30-2001||07:05 AM||||My brother-in-law has a sand and gravel biz and about a 7 acre ocean side lot.  They sometimes bury whales there as he has the gear.  They buried a 40 footer with the idea of digging it up and displaying the skeleton in a museum.<P>This summer they had an interview with a fisherman there.  He was out and saw a humpback (30-35 foot) thrashing in the water.  Getting closer he finds a pod of about six killer whales attacking it.  He said they could grab and twist the big whale almost completely out of the water.  Then decided, hey, my boat is only 30 feet long.....time to go home.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary||||reg||1
